<header class="page-head"><h1>Ingtalk Terms of Service</h1><p class="effective">Effective: August 23, 2026</p></header>
<h2>1. Purpose</h2><p>These Terms govern use of the Ingtalk service provided by Itembus and define the rights and responsibilities of the operator and users.</p>
<h2>2. Eligibility</h2><p>Ingtalk is only for users age 19 or older. By using the service, users confirm that they are at least 19 and must provide an accurate age. Accounts and content may be restricted or deleted if a user provides a false age or is found to be a minor. Users must not impersonate others or abuse rewards and points through multiple accounts.</p>
<h2>3. Service</h2><p>The service includes profiles, distance-based talk cards, chat requests and acceptance, one-to-one chats, an anonymous-alias board, points, reports, and blocks. Features may change for safety, legal compliance, or improvement. Material changes will be announced in the app or on this website.</p>
<h2>4. Points</h2><ul><li>Points are digital units used for service features and cannot be exchanged for cash or property.</li><li>Check-in, talk-card, post, comment, and advertising rewards are granted only at the stated intervals.</li><li>Points obtained through abuse, system errors, or violations may be revoked.</li><li>Payment and refund terms for paid points are disclosed separately.</li></ul>
<h2>5. Prohibited Conduct</h2><ul><li>Use by minors, sexual approaches to minors, or sexual conversations with minors</li><li>Prostitution, compensated dating, illegal recordings, pornography, or requests for such content</li><li>Threats, hate, harassment, stalking, or disclosure of personal data</li><li>Fraud, requests for money, investment or loan solicitation, or contact-harvesting spam</li><li>Misuse of another person's photos, works, or personal data</li><li>Abuse of reports, points, device recovery, or disruption of the service</li><li>Conduct that violates law or the Community Guidelines</li></ul>
<h2>6. Content and Enforcement</h2><p>Users must hold the rights necessary for content they submit. The operator may hide or remove prohibited content and suspend or permanently restrict accounts following reports, automated filters, or safety reviews. Relevant records may be preserved or disclosed in response to an immediate safety risk or lawful request.</p>
<h2>7. Reports and Appeals</h2><p>Posts, comments, users, and chats can be reported in the app. Appeals may be sent to <a href="mailto:itembus@itembus.com">itembus@itembus.com</a>.</p>
<h2>8. Account and Data Deletion</h2><p>Users may request account deletion in the app. User-facing data is deleted, while minimum information required for fraud prevention, reports, legal duties, or disputes may be isolated and retained for the period stated in the Privacy Policy. See <a href="<%=LangUrl("deletion.asp")%>">Account &amp; Data Deletion</a>.</p>
<h2>9. Limitation of Liability</h2><p>The operator does not broker or guarantee offline meetings, financial transactions, or external services between users. Users should use care when sharing personal information or meeting offline. Liability that cannot be excluded by law remains unaffected.</p>
<h2>10. Governing Law</h2><p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Korea. Disputes will be handled by a court with jurisdiction under Korean civil procedure law.</p>
